msgid "Fill the recording sheet"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Read the recording sheet of a stratigraphic unit and fill its boxes, "
"each one written into the graph.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The **Sheet** window shows a stratigraphic unit as the recording sheet of"
" an excavation standard, box by box, with the layout of the paper form. "
"The sheet is a way of reading the graph, not a second copy of the data: "
"every box reads its value from the graph, and every value you write in a "
"box goes into the graph as a description, a property, a relation or a "
"node. EMStudio comes with the Italian sheet **ICCD US 2021**, defined by "
"stratigraph-templates, the same definition that StratiField reads in the "
"field."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open a study, for example a copy of Templu Mare (see :doc:`/tutorial"
"/first-study`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The sheet is drawn for stratigraphic units (SU, USV and the other unit "
"types). Other nodes, such as documents or properties, have no sheet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open the sheet of a unit"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Sheets workspace with the recording sheet of SU004: the head, the "
"boxes filled from the graph, the boxes outside the graph hatched."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose the **Sheets** workspace in the bar across the top of the window. "
"Its question is **What does the recording sheet say of this unit?**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Select a unit, for example SU004, in the **Outliner**, in the Matrix or "
"in the **3D scene**. The **Sheet** in the middle shows its recording "
"sheet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The other windows follow the same unit: the **3D scene** frames its "
"proxy, the **Graph** window on the right frames it in the Matrix with the"
" units it touches, and the **Viewer & card** underneath shows its "
"photographs and documents."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When you select something that is not a unit, for example a property in "
"the Matrix, the sheet stays on the last unit and says so in a line above "
"the sheet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the head and the boxes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The head of the window holds, from left to right: the definition the "
"study uses (for example **ICCD US 2021 · 4.0.0**), the name and type of "
"the unit, a count of its boxes by state (**full**, **empty**, **outside "
"the graph**, **undecided**), the status of the record, and **Print A4…** "
"(see :doc:`print-sheets`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each box is in one of these states:"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Full*: the graph says it, and the box shows the value."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Empty*: the graph could say it and does not yet. The box is a field you "
"can fill."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Outside the graph*: the definition keeps this box outside the graph, for"
" example **RESPONSIBLE BODY**, **MiC OFFICE RESPONSIBLE FOR PROTECTION** "
"and **SAMPLING**. The box is hatched and reads **not in the graph**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Undecided*: two boxes of the definition write the same place in the "
"graph, and nothing says which one a value belongs to. The box is yellow "
"and lists the candidates. In ICCD US 2021 this happens to **PERIOD** and "
"**PHASE**, which both read the first epoch of the unit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hold the pointer on a box to read where its value lives in the graph (the"
" unit's description, a property, a relation) or why it is empty. A box "
"marked **lens** reads a value that another tool wrote without the mark of"
" this sheet, for example a property of the right kind added in the "
"**Inspector**: the sheet shows it and attributes it to the box."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At the foot of the sheet, **Properties of the unit no box of this sheet "
"reads** lists the properties of the unit that have no box, with their "
"values. Nothing of the unit is hidden by the sheet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write in the boxes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click an empty or full box and write. Press :kbd:`Enter` to confirm a "
"short field. In a long text, such as **DESCRIPTION**, press :kbd:`⌘Enter`"
" (:kbd:`Ctrl+Enter` on Windows and Linux), or click outside the box."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The value goes into the graph at once. Each confirmed box is one step of "
"``Edit ▸ Undo``, and the **Inspector**, the Matrix and the **3D scene** "
"show the change."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In a box with a vocabulary, such as **CONSISTENCY**, **COLOUR** or "
"**STATE OF PRESERVATION**, the field suggests the terms of the vocabulary"
" as you type. A word that is not one of the terms is written as a word, "
"and a message says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "For **MODE OF FORMATION (nature)**, choose one of the options."
msgstr ""

msgid "Some boxes need a few words of explanation:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**DEFINITION** and **INTERPRETATION**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The definition is a short phrase, written as the value of the unit's "
"*definition* property. Under it, **Term** offers the terms of the "
"vocabulary of definitions, to classify the phrase. The interpretation is "
"written on the same property, as its description, so write the definition"
" first. Under the interpretation, **Sources:** lists the extractors, "
"combiners and documents the definition rests on; double-click one to "
"select it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**DESCRIPTION**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The description of the unit. When it repeats the definition, a line under"
" the box says so: the description says what is seen."
msgstr ""

msgid "Boxes of places and activities"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**LOCALITY**, **AREA / BUILDING / STRUCTURE**, **TRENCH**, **ROOM / "
"FUNCTIONAL UNIT** and **ACTIVITY** tie the unit to a node of the graph. "
"Write its name: EMStudio finds the node with that name, or creates it, "
"and a message says that it was created."
msgstr ""

msgid "Persons"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The boxes of persons, such as **FIELD RECORDER**, take the name of a "
"person already in the graph, and point to that node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dates and the year"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**YEAR** ties the unit to the excavation of that year. **DATE OF FIELD "
"RECORDING** and **DATE OF REVISION** are written as dates (YYYY-MM-DD) on"
" an act of recording or of revision of the unit, created the first time; "
"the responsible of each act is written after its date."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write the relations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The boxes of relations, such as **COVERS**, **CUT BY** or **EARLIER "
"THAN**, show one chip for each unit in that relation. Each chip is a "
"connector of the Matrix."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To add a relation, click the **+** field of the box, write the name or "
"the number of the other unit, for example SU001, and press :kbd:`Enter`. "
"One connector is written, in the direction the box says: **COVERS** SU001"
" means that this unit covers SU001. The other unit's sheet shows the "
"inverse relation, and the Matrix on the right shows the new connector."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To remove a relation, press **×** on its chip. The connector goes, from "
"both sheets."
msgstr ""

msgid "Double-click a chip to select that unit and read its sheet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The sheet checks a relation as the Matrix does. It writes only relations "
"that the datamodel admits between the two types of unit, and it creates "
"no unit: a name that matches no unit, or a number that could be several "
"units, is refused with a message that says why. A relation that closes a "
"cycle is written, and the message names the cycle, which the Matrix draws"
" in red (see :doc:`/how-to/stratigraphy/check-the-chronology`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What stays read only"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hold the pointer on a read-only box to read the reason. In ICCD US 2021:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the number of the unit (**SU**) is its name: rename the unit in the "
"**Inspector**;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**MODE OF FORMATION (sign)** is the type of the unit, decided when the "
"unit is created;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**PERIOD** and **PHASE** are the epoch of the unit: move the unit to "
"another epoch in the Matrix (see :doc:`/how-to/stratigraphy/edit-many-"
"units`);"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the lists of rows, such as **ELEVATIONS** and **MEASUREMENTS**, and the "
"lists of documents, such as **PLANS** and **PHOTOGRAPHS**, show what the "
"graph holds; their rows are written in the **Inspector** of the unit, and"
" its pictures and documents as described in :doc:`/how-to/sources"
"/documents-and-media`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Set the status of the record"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The menu in the head, **status: not said** until you choose, records "
"whether the sheet is still **from the field** or **revised**. The choice "
"is written on the unit, and it is one of the criteria for printing (see "
":doc:`print-sheets`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose the definition of the study"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first menu of the head chooses the recording-sheet definition the "
"study uses. The choice is kept in the study, so it travels with the file,"
" and it is one step of ``Edit ▸ Undo``. A study that names none uses ICCD"
" US 2021. Definitions brought by community packages appear in the same "
"menu, with the name of their package (see :doc:`/how-to/extensions"
"/install-packages-and-plugins`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The labels of the boxes are those of the definition, in the language of "
"the interface when the definition has it. ICCD US 2021 has Italian and "
"English; in the other languages its labels are Italian, and a line above "
"the sheet says so."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The recording sheet of the unit, filled from the graph and written back "
"into it: descriptions, properties, places, acts and relations that every "
"other window of EMStudio reads, that the file keeps when you save it, and"
" that StratiField reads with the same definition."
msgstr ""

